/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 81 0 R
/T (Inventory decisions are usually made on averages and intuition. Too little stock causes lost sales and unhappy customers; too much stock blocks working capital and increases storage cost. Both problems exist together in the same business, in different SKUs and at different times of the year. FORESIGHT answers three questions: what will sell, what will run out, and what is sitting unsold.)
/E (Inventory decisions are usually made on averages and intuition. Too little stock causes lost sales and unhappy customers; too much stock blocks working capital and increases storage cost. Both problems exist together in the same business, in different SKUs and at different times of the year. FORESIGHT answers three questions: what will sell, what will run out, and what is sitting unsold.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
